#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183885 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9ceefc-3aa8-5c13-90a1-e4a084f720cc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1c04b787-534d-588e-8f53-55dd81ca5fd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14041" :question/problem "Sketch the solutions to the inequality $x+2y < 4$ in the $xy$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x + 2y & < 4 \\\\ 2y & < - x + 4 \\\\ y & < - \\frac{1}{2}x + 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves a 'strictly less than' sign, the line\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\nitself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n\nThen, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality\n\n$$\ny < -\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\nrefers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line\n\n$$\ny = -\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\nso we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/eea9bbe3f74a8d4df15c497ee51991b6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183886 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "031f0fd6-385d-56b8-9e8e-b264e6e89ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Non-Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "845cd3b6-4a16-5501-b031-d57c4bb89457" :question/math-academy-id "e-14047" :question/problem "Sketch the solutions to the inequality $-x-y \\leq -1$ in the $xy$-plane." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-x - y & \\le - 1 \\\\ -y & \\le x - 1 \\\\ y & \\ge - x + 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line\n\n$$\ny=-x+1\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves a 'greater than *or equal to*' sign, the line\n\n$$\ny=-x+1\n$$\n\nitself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a *solid line*.\n\nThen, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality\n\n$$\ny \\geq -x+1\n$$\n\nrefers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line\n\n$$\ny=-x+1\n$$\n\nso we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/c0cf262705b842b59fc8f287c310b7c8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183888 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities Involving Horizontal and Vertical Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "dc1ba796-5508-5697-a7ac-2cad5c767ffa" :question/math-academy-id "e-14056" :question/problem "Find the inequality that describes the shaded region shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/43fad45f1d96c5e8626ab609a68bfd59.png)" :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-1,0)$. Therefore, the line has the equation $x=-1$.\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use.\n\n- Since the line is *dashed*, we will use a *strict* inequality.\n- Since the shaded region is to the *right* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $x=-1$.\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n$x > -1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities Involving Horizontal and Vertical Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e7e6be5-fcec-5ddd-b8fd-3a9858fdd4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y > - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182969} {:answer/id #uuid "bff8dfbd-a150-5171-8d51-684ea0bff1fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182970} {:answer/id #uuid "2f535254-3173-5d4a-8af9-ceebc5372716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y \\le - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182971} {:answer/id #uuid "347bc70b-a147-5285-945c-8f101a52342c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y < x - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182972} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7479d8-7dee-551a-839a-ae78644b1bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x > - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f7479d8-7dee-551a-839a-ae78644b1bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x > - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182973} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e4ff889-23e6-508c-b9c3-5b46b80e0a00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182968}] :question/id #uuid "ece6fc50-0ed1-527d-8b93-8f3b5d41e6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-29423" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-29423.png)\n\nFind the inequality that describes the shaded region shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9ceefc-3aa8-5c13-90a1-e4a084f720cc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4e32104-d791-5438-ab97-4cc9b0bfa82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183468} {:answer/id #uuid "d541815a-4985-59b1-929a-ffbfe0ee47af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183469} {:answer/id #uuid "eba996f7-152f-5f25-986d-6dc1fa776e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a